    distills: >-
      One Deferred row, added because the same epic-gate review that found the refusal bug also
      verified a second cost and this close had not surfaced it: BodyViewer's JSON/XML over-cap
      fallback renders TextRenderer with no size prop, so byteLength re-encodes the whole body - up
      to the 10 MiB capture cap - on every render, which is exactly the cost W3 removed on the text
      dispatch only. The row states the mechanism, why it is not the one-line fix it looks like
      (Dispatch feeds those kinds through the lossy bodyText, so there is no whole flag to gate a
      size with, and passing one blindly would print a wrong total for a non-UTF-8 body - the
      CutMarker inversion W3's own round 1 fixed), and the condition on fixing it: the bench is
      extended first, because this epic's discipline is that a performance fix lands behind a
      measurement. It also records the trail - W3 addressed the re-decode to whoever next opened
      BodyViewer, W9 opened it for the relabel and did not carry it, and the gate is what caught it.
